## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- Migration `20260822000000_club_user_creation.sql` adds `clubs.owner_id`
  (nullable, so system/legacy clubs keep working), `clubs.posting_mode`
  (`OPEN` default, CHECK `OPEN|OWNER_ONLY`) and `clubs.cover_image`; creates the
  dedicated public bucket `club-covers` (5242880 bytes, `image/webp` only) with
  four owner-folder policies; adds `clubs_cover_image_vinea_check`; adds two
  BEFORE INSERT guards enforcing OWNER_ONLY on `club_posts` and
  `club_post_risposte`; creates `public.club_crea`; and rebuilds `public_clubs`
  with `drop view` + `create view`, because `create or replace view` cannot
  insert columns into an existing column list.
- `public.club_crea(p_nome text, p_descrizione text, p_regole text[],
  p_posting_mode text, p_cover_image text) returns public.clubs` is
  `SECURITY DEFINER` with `search_path = public`, revoked from `public` and
  granted only to `authenticated`. Its measured ACL is
  `{postgres=X, service_role=X, authenticated=X}`, the same shape as
  `segnalazione_invia`; `anon` has no execute. It requires `auth.uid()`, an
  existing profile and a non-suspended, non-removed account; consumes the
  rate-limit bucket `club:crea` at 5/hour per user; validates nome,
  descrizione, regole, posting_mode and the cover path; assigns
  `owner_id = auth.uid()`; generates the slug server-side with progressive
  numeric suffixes on collision; and inserts the creator's `club_memberships`
  row in the same transaction. `clubs` has no client INSERT grant.
- Cover references are stored as the path `<uid>/<uuid>.webp`, never an HTTP
  URL. The DB CHECK, the Storage policy regex, the RPC regex and
  `coverSicura()` agree on the same anchored form; the public origin is
  recomposed from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and fails closed when it is
  missing or not an HTTP origin.
- The frontend flow is prepare, upload, call `club_crea`, and delete the
  just-created object when the RPC fails. Preset Vinea covers are prepared and
  uploaded like any other cover, so the database holds one reference format.
  Covers are decoded, redrawn and re-encoded as WebP, so original metadata does
  not survive; there is no manual crop editor.
- `Circolo Vinea` is renamed to `Club Vinea` as a display name only; the
  historical slug `circolo-vinea` and all technical identifiers are unchanged.
- `supabase/tests/12d_club_creazione_utente.sql` WAS EXECUTED on 2026-08-24 on
  PostgreSQL 17.10 in a disposable container, from empty, with the 9c bootstrap
  and all 35 repository migrations applied in order, each in its own
  transaction: first run 47 pass / 1 fail, second and definitive run
